"Reports come from VATSIM's METAR service, the same source the tracker has always used, and each station issues one an hour. Where a field files none — which is most of the world's airfields — the reading is Open-Meteo's model, and says so; the same request carries the forecast and the outlook, and the sun and moon times are worked out on the device. Severe-weather warnings come from the National Weather Service, which covers the United States and nowhere else. The radar tiles are RainViewer's; the satellite imagery is from NASA's Global Imagery Browse Services, part of their Earth Science Data and Information System; the winds aloft are Open-Meteo's too. None of it costs anything to use." = "Reports come from VATSIM's METAR service, the same source the tracker has always used, and each station issues one an hour. Where a field files none — which is most of the world's airfields — the reading is Open-Meteo's model, and says so; the same request carries the forecast and the outlook, and the sun and moon times are worked out on the device. Severe-weather warnings come from the National Weather Service, which covers the United States and nowhere else. The radar tiles are RainViewer's; the satellite imagery is from NASA's Global Imagery Browse Services, part of their Earth Science Data and Information System; the winds aloft are Open-Meteo's too. None of it costs anything to use.";
